00:18:05,892 --> 00:18:07,838
Let the party spokesperson
make the announcement.

257
00:18:07,838 --> 00:18:10,212
Weechana doesn't have to do anything
or appear in public.

258
00:18:10,212 --> 00:18:12,022
That's it.

259
00:18:12,889 --> 00:18:15,262
I'm with Weechai on this.

260
00:18:18,713 --> 00:18:21,102
We need to get it done in two hours.

261
00:18:42,915 --> 00:18:44,953
Boat, what's up?

262
00:18:44,953 --> 00:18:45,679
<i>Did you see?</i>

263
00:18:45,680 --> 00:18:48,782
<i>Weechana's side is pushing back,
saying Eva's video was AI-generated.</i>

264
00:18:48,782 --> 00:18:50,393
What?

265
00:18:50,393 --> 00:18:52,152
And people believed that?

266
00:18:52,152 --> 00:18:53,601
<i>People are split on this.</i>

267
00:18:53,601 --> 00:18:57,206
<i>The party's bots must be working overtime.</i>

268
00:18:59,249 --> 00:19:03,902
How is my aunt? Can I talk to her?

269
00:19:04,769 --> 00:19:07,020
<i>She went to the provincial fair with my mom.</i>

270
00:19:07,020 --> 00:19:08,844
The whole street went together.

271
00:19:08,844 --> 00:19:10,454
They all got dressed up for it too.

272
00:19:10,454 --> 00:19:12,702
The moms are having fun.

273
00:19:15,062 --> 00:19:17,053
<i>Don't worry.</i>

274
00:19:17,053 --> 00:19:18,800
She is safe here.

275
00:19:18,800 --> 00:19:21,782
My mom practically runs this neighborhood.

276
00:19:23,166 --> 00:19:26,457
Okay, thanks for taking care of her.

277
00:19:26,457 --> 00:19:27,988
<i>Pun.</i>

278
00:19:27,988 --> 00:19:30,036
What's up?

279
00:19:30,036 --> 00:19:33,028
If you need me, just call.

280
00:19:33,028 --> 00:19:35,753
I'm always down to throw hands for you.

281
00:19:35,753 --> 00:19:37,182
<i>Okay?</i>

282
00:19:37,182 --> 00:19:39,622
Okay. Talk to you later.

283
00:19:45,120 --> 00:19:48,200
[Official statement
from the Ruam Thai Chana Party]

284
00:19:48,480 --> 00:19:50,368
<i>At this crucial final stage of the campaign,</i>

285
00:19:50,369 --> 00:19:51,872
<i>we never expected to be targeted</i>

286
00:19:51,872 --> 00:19:54,476
<i>with false information
and AI-generated fake media.</i>

287
00:19:54,476 --> 00:19:56,604
<i>We urge everyone
not to let fabricated content</i>

288
00:19:56,604 --> 00:20:01,409
<i>overshadow Weechana's
genuine commitment and good intentions.</i>

289
00:20:01,409 --> 00:20:03,554
<i>Our party will continue moving forward
and doing our duty.</i>

290
00:20:03,554 --> 00:20:07,826
<i>And we want to make one thing clear:
Choose the truth. Choose a better future.</i>

291
00:20:07,826 --> 00:20:10,222
I'll show you an even bigger truth.

292
00:20:39,036 --> 00:20:40,305
Please wait for a minute.

293
00:20:40,305 --> 00:20:43,612
I told the reporters we only have 15 minutes.

294
00:20:43,612 --> 00:20:44,767
Sure.

295
00:20:44,767 --> 00:20:46,568
I'm not in a hurry.

296
00:20:51,120 --> 00:20:52,828
I'm ready, let's go.

297
00:20:52,828 --> 00:20:53,680
How do you feel

298
00:20:53,680 --> 00:20:57,062
about all the news
surrounding the Ruam Thai Chana Party?

299
00:20:57,760 --> 00:21:00,035
You're not going to ask me about my work?

300
00:21:00,036 --> 00:21:03,668
Actually, I've got two more series coming up.

301
00:21:03,668 --> 00:21:06,478
Are they like period dramas or something?

302
00:21:06,478 --> 00:21:09,358
That's right.
The production quality is really high.

303
00:21:09,358 --> 00:21:12,857
Do you have a party in mind
for this election?

304
00:21:12,857 --> 00:21:14,858
Do you still have faith in Weechana?

305
00:21:14,858 --> 00:21:16,969
And have you ever experienced anything
like what Eva went through?

306
00:21:16,969 --> 00:21:19,886
Have you talked to Weechai
since the news came out?

307
00:21:19,886 --> 00:21:22,724
What's your relationship with Weechai like
right now?

308
00:21:22,724 --> 00:21:25,420
- How are things between you two right now?
- Please answer my question.

309
00:21:25,420 --> 00:21:28,454
- Can you tell us something?
- Sorry, everyone.

310
00:21:28,454 --> 00:21:30,942
She won't be commenting on politics.

311
00:21:30,942 --> 00:21:32,977
So she's going with
the "ignorance is bliss" approach?

312
00:21:32,977 --> 00:21:36,697
Being a celebrity doesn't mean
you have to stay out of politics.

313
00:21:36,697 --> 00:21:38,724
No, it's not like that.

314
00:21:38,724 --> 00:21:42,462
Let's stick to questions
about the brand, please.

315
00:21:42,462 --> 00:21:46,092
- The product is really great.
- Can you say something about it?

316
00:21:46,092 --> 00:21:52,124
Let's talk about her period drama,
she was really pretty in it.

317
00:21:58,025 --> 00:21:59,860
Some of the reporters
are still hanging around.

318
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:01,321
You know, the really persistent ones.

319
00:22:01,321 --> 00:22:04,422
They probably saw Weechai here
and decided to wait around.

320
00:22:06,140 --> 00:22:10,470
And since Weechana hasn't made
any moves this time,

321
00:22:10,470 --> 00:22:12,524
they're all coming
after his younger brother instead.

322
00:22:12,524 --> 00:22:14,325
Come on.

323
00:22:18,209 --> 00:22:21,766
I think I... I'll go take a look outside.

324
00:22:21,766 --> 00:22:24,001
I'll call you if the coast is clear.

325
00:22:31,318 --> 00:22:33,222
I'm sorry.

326
00:22:35,718 --> 00:22:38,022
I never wanted to put you through
any of this.

327
00:22:41,748 --> 00:22:44,862
Lately, no one even asks me
about my work anymore.

328
00:22:46,137 --> 00:22:48,590
Ever since I went campaigning with you,

329
00:22:48,590 --> 00:22:51,940
all I've been getting are hate comments.

330
00:22:51,940 --> 00:22:55,844
At this point, more people are blocking me
than following me.

331
00:23:01,254 --> 00:23:03,422
We should just go.

332
00:23:04,854 --> 00:23:07,324
I'm not having fun anymore.

333
00:23:08,454 --> 00:23:10,255
Pie.

334
00:23:10,998 --> 00:23:13,452
I really can't leave my family behind.

335
00:23:14,145 --> 00:23:16,838
The family
that makes you look like the bad guy?

336
00:23:18,652 --> 00:23:21,502
How much more shit
are you gonna take for them?

337
00:23:23,590 --> 00:23:26,766
Once people have made up their minds
about you,

338
00:23:26,766 --> 00:23:29,465
it's hard...

339
00:23:29,465 --> 00:23:34,385
it's really really hard
to change the way they see you.

340
00:23:34,385 --> 00:23:35,945
Why?

341
00:23:35,945 --> 00:23:38,890
Are you just gonna keep playing the bad guy?

342
00:23:42,577 --> 00:23:44,662
We should leave all of this behind.

343
00:23:45,857 --> 00:23:48,444
We can go somewhere you feel comfortable
and start over.

344
00:23:51,902 --> 00:23:54,422
You know,
I've actually always wanted to be a model.

345
00:23:55,993 --> 00:23:59,550
I don't eat much. You can afford to feed me.

346
00:24:15,217 --> 00:24:17,168
Another video just got leaked.

347
00:24:17,168 --> 00:24:18,569
Huh?

348
00:24:23,476 --> 00:24:25,302
It's the video from that night.

349
00:24:29,157 --> 00:24:32,542
Yeah, I saw it. I'll be right there.

350
00:24:34,769 --> 00:24:36,358
Pie,

351
00:24:36,358 --> 00:24:39,105
find another way out.
Don't let the reporters see you.

352
00:24:39,105 --> 00:24:42,238
If you're done with work,
just go home and wait for me there.

353
00:24:42,238 --> 00:24:44,777
I'll come meet you there
as soon as I get everything sorted out.

354
00:24:44,777 --> 00:24:47,449
- And then we...
- No!

355
00:24:47,449 --> 00:24:49,250
I'm leaving now.

356
00:24:49,940 --> 00:24:52,222
If you have to keep running back
to deal with your family,

357
00:24:52,222 --> 00:24:54,401
I'm not waiting around anymore.

358
00:24:54,401 --> 00:24:55,421
I'm leaving.

359
00:24:55,421 --> 00:24:59,082
Pie, calm down.

360
00:24:59,950 --> 00:25:02,124
We'll go together.

361
00:25:02,124 --> 00:25:04,236
Just let me help my family first, okay?

362
00:25:04,236 --> 00:25:06,662
You seriously still call them your family?

363
00:25:08,134 --> 00:25:09,781
Babe...

364
00:25:11,062 --> 00:25:14,182
Your family should make you
feel good about who you are,

365
00:25:16,673 --> 00:25:18,474
not like this.

366
00:25:40,958 --> 00:25:43,302
It's your life, babe.

367
00:26:14,154 --> 00:26:15,881
What are you doing out here?

368
00:26:16,686 --> 00:26:18,742
You've been here for a while now.

369
00:26:20,070 --> 00:26:21,702
You want your phone back?

370
00:26:21,702 --> 00:26:24,380
No, I'm not here to get my phone back.

371
00:26:24,380 --> 00:26:26,181
I came to call you for dinner.

372
00:26:26,966 --> 00:26:28,902
I'm not really hungry.

373
00:26:29,542 --> 00:26:32,049
You need to eat,
or you'll start losing muscle.

374
00:26:32,049 --> 00:26:33,846
You have to eat, come on.

375
00:26:33,846 --> 00:26:35,862
Jim makes an amazing steak.

376
00:26:45,496 --> 00:26:47,816
Okay, let's go.

377
00:26:56,004 --> 00:26:57,805
Do you like me?

378
00:27:06,466 --> 00:27:08,285
What?

379
00:27:09,636 --> 00:27:11,462
That's all you can say?

380
00:27:16,292 --> 00:27:17,747
Yes.

381
00:27:19,454 --> 00:27:21,710
Yes, I like you.

382
00:27:21,710 --> 00:27:24,342
Yes, I like all of you.

383
00:27:24,953 --> 00:27:26,758
I like you when you're just you.

384
00:27:26,758 --> 00:27:28,465
I like you
when you let yourself be vulnerable.

385
00:27:28,465 --> 00:27:30,598
I like you when you cry.

386
00:27:30,598 --> 00:27:32,764
Well, I don't like seeing you cry.

387
00:27:32,764 --> 00:27:35,422
I just like that you let yourself cry.

388
00:27:36,697 --> 00:27:40,622
I even like you
when you're being stubborn and unreasonable.

389
00:27:42,158 --> 00:27:44,742
I like that you know what you want.

390
00:27:46,073 --> 00:27:48,182
I like your dreams, too.

391
00:27:52,067 --> 00:27:53,868
Oh, I really like you.

392
00:27:55,968 --> 00:27:59,703
And... I like watching you act, too.

393
00:28:02,028 --> 00:28:04,622
Yeah, I've been secretly watching your stuff.

394
00:28:05,446 --> 00:28:07,247
And I think you are...

395
00:28:10,686 --> 00:28:12,487
You're incredible.

396
00:28:13,177 --> 00:28:15,822
You're so talented.

397
00:28:17,302 --> 00:28:19,484
And...

398
00:28:19,484 --> 00:28:25,462
I know I don't deserve to be by your side.

399
00:28:27,649 --> 00:28:30,502
But I can't stop how I feel.

400
00:28:36,319 --> 00:28:37,903
I...

401
00:28:42,379 --> 00:28:43,973
I'm sorry.

402
00:28:46,398 --> 00:28:50,202
Look, if any of that made you uncomfortable,

403
00:28:50,202 --> 00:28:51,873
I'm sorry.

404
00:28:51,873 --> 00:28:53,548
Just forget I said it.

405
00:28:53,548 --> 00:28:58,070
I swear I'll never
make you feel uncomfortable.

406
00:28:59,126 --> 00:29:01,692
We can still be friends.

407
00:29:01,692 --> 00:29:03,937
I will do anything for you.

408
00:29:03,937 --> 00:29:07,382
I'll be whatever you need me to be.

409
00:29:08,710 --> 00:29:10,511
I swear.

410
00:29:15,206 --> 00:29:17,007
Then... how about...

411
00:29:20,302 --> 00:29:22,103
being my friend...

412
00:29:25,369 --> 00:29:27,622
and my boyfriend?

413
00:29:34,049 --> 00:29:38,070
One more time, just to be sure.

414
00:29:38,070 --> 00:29:41,222
I said both, be my friend and my boyfriend.
What's so hard to understand?

415
00:30:16,742 --> 00:30:19,943
Before I lose all my courage,

416
00:30:20,604 --> 00:30:22,405
may I kiss you?

417
00:31:19,777 --> 00:31:21,225
Shall we?

418
00:31:35,422 --> 00:31:37,223
We need to do something.

419
00:31:38,441 --> 00:31:39,992
Oh, no. Dad.

420
00:31:39,992 --> 00:31:43,422
Do you know if she has any other videos?

421
00:31:44,396 --> 00:31:48,593
What if she has something we can't deny?
What are we gonna do then?

422
00:31:54,652 --> 00:31:59,566
What do you mean by,
"we need to do something"?

423
00:31:59,566 --> 00:32:02,542
Track Eva down as soon as possible.

424
00:32:02,542 --> 00:32:05,702
Bring her in and keep her somewhere
until the campaign is over.

425
00:32:06,636 --> 00:32:08,462
By "keep her",

426
00:32:09,196 --> 00:32:12,209
- you mean here?
- Anywhere.

427
00:32:12,209 --> 00:32:15,142
As long as it's somewhere
we can keep her under control.

428
00:32:16,836 --> 00:32:20,910
And if Eva causes any more trouble,

429
00:32:20,910 --> 00:32:24,116
I'll have to put out a story
that she's gone abroad...

430
00:32:24,116 --> 00:32:25,673
and then she'll simply disappear.

431
00:32:25,673 --> 00:32:27,474
No, Dad.

432
00:32:28,846 --> 00:32:31,140
We don't have to go that far.

433
00:32:31,140 --> 00:32:34,238
I can talk to her. I think I can handle her.

434
00:32:34,238 --> 00:32:36,873
We just need to find her
and sit down with her.

435
00:32:36,873 --> 00:32:40,020
I'm sure I can get her back on our side.

436
00:32:40,020 --> 00:32:41,822
Trust me, Dad.

437
00:32:45,121 --> 00:32:46,922
Dad?

438
00:32:49,884 --> 00:32:52,222
I used to believe that too.

439
00:32:54,254 --> 00:32:56,055
But in the end,

440
00:32:57,220 --> 00:32:59,342
you can't change people.

441
00:33:02,308 --> 00:33:04,422
You're talking about my mom,

442
00:33:07,894 --> 00:33:09,862
aren't you?

443
00:33:20,377 --> 00:33:22,742
When you said that just now...

444
00:33:22,742 --> 00:33:24,926
were you talking about my mom?

445
00:33:24,926 --> 00:33:26,628
Weechai, come on.

446
00:33:26,628 --> 00:33:28,313
Weechai! Weechai!

447
00:33:28,313 --> 00:33:31,222
I asked you a question.

448
00:33:31,222 --> 00:33:33,262
Were you talking about my mom?

449
00:33:34,742 --> 00:33:36,553
Tell me!

450
00:33:36,553 --> 00:33:38,457
Just tell me.

451
00:33:38,457 --> 00:33:40,462
Were you talking about my mom?

452
00:34:41,212 --> 00:34:45,121
Send someone to whoever runs that page.

453
00:34:45,121 --> 00:34:48,188
Pressure them until they tell us
where Eva is.

454
00:34:48,188 --> 00:34:50,142
Yes, ma'am.

455
00:34:50,142 --> 00:34:53,726
I want our people
to get to Eva as soon as possible.

456
00:34:53,726 --> 00:34:58,611
There's a special reward
for whoever brings her in.

457
00:34:58,611 --> 00:35:00,502
Yes, ma'am.

458
00:35:38,817 --> 00:35:41,233
Are you a stalker?

459
00:35:41,233 --> 00:35:44,038
- What?
- Are you a stalker?

460
00:35:44,038 --> 00:35:46,502
Yeah. Yes, I am.

461
00:35:50,372 --> 00:35:52,158
How long have you been up?

462
00:35:52,158 --> 00:35:53,836
For a while.

463
00:35:53,836 --> 00:35:56,009
I've just been watching you sleep.

464
00:35:58,422 --> 00:36:00,369
And thinking about...

465
00:36:00,369 --> 00:36:03,601
how I can take even better care of you.

466
00:36:05,793 --> 00:36:09,382
You already take good care of me.

467
00:36:11,180 --> 00:36:12,981
Eva.

468
00:36:13,740 --> 00:36:18,540
We can't keep running forever.

469
00:36:18,540 --> 00:36:20,662
This isn't good for you.

470
00:36:22,257 --> 00:36:24,886
You have your own life,

471
00:36:24,886 --> 00:36:28,822
your own dreams,
and important work waiting for you.

472
00:36:29,803 --> 00:36:31,604
I...

473
00:36:33,334 --> 00:36:36,542
I think we need to find a way
to stand up to Weechana.

474
00:36:38,006 --> 00:36:42,142
Have you figured out our next move?

475
00:36:44,204 --> 00:36:47,942
I think there might be a way.

476
00:36:48,710 --> 00:36:50,817
But...

477
00:36:50,817 --> 00:36:53,201
I'm just worried
it could be too risky for you.

478
00:36:57,132 --> 00:36:59,484
Don't worry about me.

479
00:36:59,484 --> 00:37:01,569
I don't think Weechana would hurt me.

480
00:37:02,534 --> 00:37:04,689
But you're right.

481
00:37:06,254 --> 00:37:08,882
We can't keep running forever.

482
00:37:10,979 --> 00:37:12,841
Okay.

483
00:37:12,841 --> 00:37:18,822
Well, I just need you to trust me.

484
00:37:21,396 --> 00:37:23,620
Of course, I trust you.

485
00:37:32,825 --> 00:37:34,742
This is how we're going to begin.

486
00:37:35,652 --> 00:37:38,062
My plan is...
